(6194558, 913574, 79720, '<td valign="top">Sorry there weren''t any challenge comments for you, Brian. Generally, that''s an indication that although you met the challenge parameters, there wasn''t anything to either like or dislike with the entry. In this case, you''ve managed to ably demonstrate a fill technique, but there aren''t any overly engaging elements to the image. The colours seem just a bit flat (you might try to play with a "curves" layer to increase the contrast), and the candid nature of the image leaves you with little room to play with composition. I scored this one a 5.<br/> <br/>Considering you''re approaching your 500th challenge entry, and your profile is filled with 6.5+ entries, I''m sure you''ve heard all this before.</td>', 'Sorry there weren''t any challenge comments for you, Brian. Generally, that''s an indication that although you met the challenge parameters, there wasn''t anything to either like or dislike with the entry. In this case, you''ve managed to ably demonstrate a fill technique, but there aren''t any overly engaging elements to the image. The colours seem just a bit flat (you might try to play with a "curves" layer to increase the contrast), and the candid nature of the image leaves you with little room to play with composition. I scored this one a 5. Considering you''re approaching your 500th challenge entry, and your profile is filled with 6.5+ entries, I''m sure you''ve heard all this before.', '2010-10-18 10:15:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(6194566, 913683, 103411, '<td valign="top">Wow dude, very nice.  Really becoming a fan of your work.</td>', 'Wow dude, very nice.  Really becoming a fan of your work.', '2010-10-18 10:23:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6194568, 913677, 33352, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the Blue, but with the flash shadows being thrown backwards it is not really fill flash, as fill flash is to nuetralise the forground with the background light with no shadows.</td>', 'Congratulations on the Blue, but with the flash shadows being thrown backwards it is not really fill flash, as fill flash is to nuetralise the forground with the background light with no shadows.', '2010-10-18 10:26:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6194571, 913683, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by snaffles:</b></div><hr/><i> Are you sure you''ve only been into photography for about a year or so, Christophe?  Great use of lighting, wonderful outfit, cute model...great take on a classic pose and congrats on the ribbon! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks :-)<br/>All I can say is that DPC is a fantastic place to learn photography. Just look at my very first photos on my <a href="//www.flickr.com/gyaban_fr/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">flickr account</a>... I was proud of them at the time! ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by snaffles: Are you sure you''ve only been into photography for about a year or so, Christophe?  Great use of lighting, wonderful outfit, cute model...great take on a classic pose and congrats on the ribbon!   Thanks :-)All I can say is that DPC is a fantastic place to learn photography. Just look at my very first photos on my flickr account... I was proud of them at the time! ;-)', '2010-10-18 10:33:26.000000', NULL, 0),
